│ Okay, let's address this issue. The core     │
│ problem is that the deletion.Collector isn't │
│ combining delete queries effectively when    │
│ emulating ON DELETE CASCADE. The current     │
│ implementation performs individual DELETE    │
│ queries for each foreign key relationship,   │
│ leading to inefficiency. The goal is to      │
│ modify perform_fast_queries to combine these │
│ queries into a single, more efficient DELETE │
│ statement using OR.                          │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The perform_fast_queries method within       │
│ deletion.Collector currently iterates        │
│ through the foreign key relationships and    │
│ executes individual DELETE queries. To       │
│ address the issue, we need to modify this    │
│ method to construct a single DELETE          │
│ statement that includes all related records  │
│ using an OR condition. This will             │
│ significantly reduce the number of database  │
│ roundtrips.  We'll focus on modifying the    │
│ logic within perform_fast_queries to achieve │
│ this combination.                            │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]deletion/collector.py[/file]          │
│  [original] def perform_fast_queries(self,   │
│  model_class, obj):                          │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│      for related_obj in                      │
│  model_class.objects.filter(pk__in=related_  │
│  s):                                         │
│          self.collector.add(self.create_del  │
│  e_query(related_obj))                       │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched] def perform_fast_queries(self,    │
│  model_class, obj):                          │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│      related_ids = getattr(obj, 'friends',   │
│  []).all().values_list('id', flat=True)      │
│      if related_ids:                         │
│          query = db.connection.cursor()      │
│          query.execute(f"DELETE FROM         │
│  {model_class._meta.db_table} WHERE id IN    │
│  ({','.join(['%s'] * len(related_ids))}) OR  │
│  friends__id IN ({','.join(['%s'] *          │
│  len(related_ids))})")                       │
│          query.executemany('%s', related_id  │
│          self.collector.add(query)           │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 2              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]deletion/collector.py[/file]          │
│  [original] def create_delete_query(self,    │
│  obj):                                       │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│      return f"DELETE FROM                    │
│  {obj._meta.db_table} WHERE id = %s"         │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched] def create_delete_query(self,     │
│  obj):                                       │
│      # ... other code ...                    │
│      return f"DELETE FROM                    │
│  {obj._meta.db_table} WHERE id = %s OR       │
│  friends__id = %s"                           │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation of Changes:                      │
│                                              │
│  • Modification 1: The perform_fast_queries  │
│    method now retrieves the IDs of related   │
│    objects using related_ids = getattr(obj,  │
│    'friends', []).all().values_list('id',    │
│    flat=True). It then constructs a single   │
│    DELETE query using db.connection.cursor() │
│    and an OR condition to include both id    │
│    and friends__id in the WHERE clause.  The │
│    executemany method is used to efficiently │
│    execute the query with multiple values.   │
│  • Modification 2: The create_delete_query   │
│    method is modified to include the OR      │
│    friends__id = %s condition in the DELETE  │
│    statement. This ensures that the query    │
│    also deletes related records through the  │
│    friends relationship.                     │
│                                              │
│ This patch addresses the core issue by       │
│ combining the individual DELETE queries into │
│ a single, more efficient query,              │
│ significantly reducing the number of         │
│ database roundtrips and improving            │
│ performance.                                 │
